# Opens Rumble from Options with no names saved, switches P1's rumble off
# and on, presses Right, which with no names does nothing, switches P1 off
# and on again to show it is still on its panel, and goes back to Options
# with B. The switches reach the save only in memory: run with no card, the
# default:
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/rumble.drive
# The drivers reach port 1 alone; a controller plugged in on another port
# adds its panel to the opening, which the wait allows. run_level.py counts
# P1's lines: four, so Right taking P1 off its panel fails it.

# Title screen to the main menu (tools/a11y/main_menu.drive).
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: game mode"
press A until "boot scene: state 0 scene 1$" 20 0.3
wait '"Main Menu\. 1-P Mode\. '
# The menu ignores input for its first 20 frames.
sleep 1

# Options, opening on Rumble.
press Down
wait '"VS\. Mode\. '
press Down
wait '"Trophies\. '
press Down
wait '"Options\. '
press A
wait '"Options\. Rumble\. '
sleep 0.3

# The opening: a new save's rumble is on.
press A
wait '"Rumble\. P1: On\. (P[2-4]: O(n|ff)\. )*A to turn on or off\. Player name entry must precede Rumble setting\."$'
# The screen ignores input until its intro has played.
sleep 1

# P1 off and on.
press A
wait '"P1: Off"$'
press A
wait '"P1: On"$'

# Right with no names: nothing, and P1 stays on its panel.
press Right
sleep 0.5
press A
wait '"P1: Off"$'
press A
wait '"P1: On"$'

# B back to Options.
press B
wait '"Options\. Rumble\. Turn the Rumble feature on or off\."'
